{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NPRbPUwQB2Y1DXPdL4hKHb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# GPU Prover Optimization Context\n2\t\n3\t## Setup\n4\t\n5\t### Repositories\n6\t\n7\t- stark-backend: https://github.com/powdr-labs/stark-backend, branch `autoopt-2026-04-10`\n8\t- openvm: https://github.com/powdr-labs/openvm, branch `v2-powdr-07-04`\n9\t- powdr: https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr, branch `openvm-v2-integration-07-04`\n10\t\n11\tThe powdr repo's Cargo.toml uses local patches for openvm and stark-backend, so all three repos must be checked out side-by-side.\n12\t\n13\t### Tools\n14\t\n15\tDownload `spec.py` for analyzing metrics files:\n16\thttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/powdr-labs/powdr/refs/heads/main/openvm/metrics-viewer/spec.py\n17\t\n18\tDownload these scripts from the powdr **main** branch (they are out-of-date on the working branch):\n19\thttps://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/tree/main/openvm-riscv/scripts\n20\t\n21\tThis includes `basic_metrics.py` for creating combined metrics files.\n22\t\n23\t## Problem Description\n24\t\n25\tWe're analyzing OpenVM v2 with autoprecompiles (APCs). Going from 0 to 300 APCs, trace cells, bus interaction messages, and constraint instances all decrease by >2x. With the CPU prover, STARK time (excl. trace) scales accordingly. With the GPU prover, it does not.\n26\t\n27\tThe goal is to make the GPU prover's \"STARK excl trace\" metric scale with the reduction in cells, bus interaction messages, and constraint instances as APCs increase (>2x improvement from APC 0 to APC 300).\n28\t\n29\tFocus ONLY on \"STARK excl trace\" — do not optimize other proving phases like trace gen or preflight execution.\n30\t\n31\tFor more context, see [this writeup](https://gist.github.com/leonardoalt/cb8fba32b08669fc63dea4d7ab0b67af).\n32\tMake sure you read it in full and explore the linked resources (e.g. the paper).\n33\t\n34\t## Measuring Results\n35\t\n36\tIn the powdr repo, run:\n37\t\n38\t```bash\n39\topenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tfor APCs {0, 100, 300}. Results go to `results/pairing/`, each config producing a `metrics.json`.\n43\t\n44\tThe script compiles the guest and generates autoprecompiles once (this is slow on the first run), then tests prover changes without recompilation.\n45\t\n46\t### Analysis Tool\n47\t\n48\tUse `spec.py` (downloaded in Setup) to analyze the metrics files:\n49\t```\n50\tpython spec.py <metrics_json_path> <experiment_name>\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\tThis gives a fine-granular breakdown of proof time. An example run:\n54\t\n55\t```\n56\t$ python spec.py https://gist.githubusercontent.com/leonardoalt/f2b810eaf2d5d37491da491f496639d1/raw/551f8590bd372dc909db3d3da2235b6a8aff70d0/metrics_pairing_v2_combined.json metrics_pairing_v2_apc300\n57\t\n58\tExperiment: metrics_pairing_v2_apc300  (OpenVM 2)\n59\t\n60\t  App Proof Basic Stats\n61\t  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n62\t  Segments                  2\n63\t  AIR Instances             623\n64\t  Columns                   106,842\n65\t  Cells                     811.18M (811,182,720)\n66\t  Constraints               54,961\n67\t  Constraint Instances      505.24M (505,240,712)\n68\t  Bus Interactions          67,357\n69\t  Bus Interaction Messages  448.46M (448,457,256)\n70\t\n71\t  Proof Time\n72\t  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n73\t  Metered Execution        0.67s (669 ms)  (  8.6%)\n74\t  App Proof Time           5.90s (5896 ms)  ( 76.1%)\n75\t    STARK (excl. trace)    2.58s (2579 ms)  ( 33.3%)\n76\t      Constraints          1.63s (1628 ms)  ( 21.0%)\n77\t        LogUp GKR          0.78s (781 ms)  ( 10.1%)\n78\t        Round 0            0.66s (662 ms)  (  8.5%)\n79\t        MLE Rounds         0.18s (182 ms)  (  2.3%)\n80\t        Other              0.00s (3 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n81\t      Openings             0.51s (514 ms)  (  6.6%)\n82\t        WHIR               0.19s (188 ms)  (  2.4%)\n83\t        Stacked Reduction  0.33s (325 ms)  (  4.2%)\n84\t        Other              0.00s (1 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n85\t      Trace Commit         0.43s (434 ms)  (  5.6%)\n86\t      Other                0.00s (3 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n87\t    Preflight Execution    1.83s (1830 ms)  ( 23.6%)\n88\t    Set Initial Memory     0.20s (203 ms)  (  2.6%)\n89\t    Trace Gen              1.28s (1282 ms)  ( 16.6%)\n90\t    Other                  0.00s (2 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n91\t  Leaf Recursion           0.50s (502 ms)  (  6.5%)\n92\t  Inner Recursion          0.41s (409 ms)  (  5.3%)\n93\t  Compression              0.27s (270 ms)  (  3.5%)\n94\t  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n95\t  Total                    7.75s (7746 ms)  (100.0%)\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\tWe would expect \"STARK (excl. trace)\" to scale with a combination of cells, bus interaction messages and constraint instances, which are all going down by a factor of >2x when going from 0 to 300 APCs. This is not the case in practice on GPU though.\n99\t\n100\t## Profiling\n101\t\n102\tNVIDIA nsight and nvidia-smi are available. Use them to understand GPU performance characteristics and bottlenecks.\n103\t\n104\t## Constraints\n105\t\n106\t- Do NOT change the underlying cryptographic protocol.\n107\t- Do NOT change the verifier.\n108\t- Do NOT optimize other proving phases, aside from \"STARK (excl. trace)\"\n109\t\n110\t## Result Files\n111\t\n112\tFor each task, collect:\n113\t- `before_apc{000,100,300}.json` — metrics before the change\n114\t- `after_apc{000,100,300}.json` — metrics after the change\n115\t- `metrics_combined.json` — created using `basic_metrics.py`\n116\t- Relevant profiling files (nsight exports, etc.)\n117\t\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dad4735-cfc3-4e75-88af-7885288c829c","uuid":"6aa15484-8d4c-4cd0-b0b6-50be321ab987","timestamp":"2026-04-11T08:03:41.392Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md","content":"# GPU Prover Optimization Context\n\n## Setup\n\n### Repositories\n\n- stark-backend: https://github.com/powdr-labs/stark-backend, branch `autoopt-2026-04-10`\n- openvm: https://github.com/powdr-labs/openvm, branch `v2-powdr-07-04`\n- powdr: https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr, branch `openvm-v2-integration-07-04`\n\nThe powdr repo's Cargo.toml uses local patches for openvm and stark-backend, so all three repos must be checked out side-by-side.\n\n### Tools\n\nDownload `spec.py` for analyzing metrics files:\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/powdr-labs/powdr/refs/heads/main/openvm/metrics-viewer/spec.py\n\nDownload these scripts from the powdr **main** branch (they are out-of-date on the working branch):\nhttps://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/tree/main/openvm-riscv/scripts\n\nThis includes `basic_metrics.py` for creating combined metrics files.\n\n## Problem Description\n\nWe're analyzing OpenVM v2 with autoprecompiles (APCs). Going from 0 to 300 APCs, trace cells, bus interaction messages, and constraint instances all decrease by >2x. With the CPU prover, STARK time (excl. trace) scales accordingly. With the GPU prover, it does not.\n\nThe goal is to make the GPU prover's \"STARK excl trace\" metric scale with the reduction in cells, bus interaction messages, and constraint instances as APCs increase (>2x improvement from APC 0 to APC 300).\n\nFocus ONLY on \"STARK excl trace\" — do not optimize other proving phases like trace gen or preflight execution.\n\nFor more context, see [this writeup](https://gist.github.com/leonardoalt/cb8fba32b08669fc63dea4d7ab0b67af).\nMake sure you read it in full and explore the linked resources (e.g. the paper).\n\n## Measuring Results\n\nIn the powdr repo, run:\n\n```bash\nopenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n```\n\nfor APCs {0, 100, 300}. Results go to `results/pairing/`, each config producing a `metrics.json`.\n\nThe script compiles the guest and generates autoprecompiles once (this is slow on the first run), then tests prover changes without recompilation.\n\n### Analysis Tool\n\nUse `spec.py` (downloaded in Setup) to analyze the metrics files:\n```\npython spec.py <metrics_json_path> <experiment_name>\n```\n\nThis gives a fine-granular breakdown of proof time. An example run:\n\n```\n$ python spec.py https://gist.githubusercontent.com/leonardoalt/f2b810eaf2d5d37491da491f496639d1/raw/551f8590bd372dc909db3d3da2235b6a8aff70d0/metrics_pairing_v2_combined.json metrics_pairing_v2_apc300\n\nExperiment: metrics_pairing_v2_apc300  (OpenVM 2)\n\n  App Proof Basic Stats\n  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Segments                  2\n  AIR Instances             623\n  Columns                   106,842\n  Cells                     811.18M (811,182,720)\n  Constraints               54,961\n  Constraint Instances      505.24M (505,240,712)\n  Bus Interactions          67,357\n  Bus Interaction Messages  448.46M (448,457,256)\n\n  Proof Time\n  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Metered Execution        0.67s (669 ms)  (  8.6%)\n  App Proof Time           5.90s (5896 ms)  ( 76.1%)\n    STARK (excl. trace)    2.58s (2579 ms)  ( 33.3%)\n      Constraints          1.63s (1628 ms)  ( 21.0%)\n        LogUp GKR          0.78s (781 ms)  ( 10.1%)\n        Round 0            0.66s (662 ms)  (  8.5%)\n        MLE Rounds         0.18s (182 ms)  (  2.3%)\n        Other              0.00s (3 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n      Openings             0.51s (514 ms)  (  6.6%)\n        WHIR               0.19s (188 ms)  (  2.4%)\n        Stacked Reduction  0.33s (325 ms)  (  4.2%)\n        Other              0.00s (1 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n      Trace Commit         0.43s (434 ms)  (  5.6%)\n      Other                0.00s (3 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n    Preflight Execution    1.83s (1830 ms)  ( 23.6%)\n    Set Initial Memory     0.20s (203 ms)  (  2.6%)\n    Trace Gen              1.28s (1282 ms)  ( 16.6%)\n    Other                  0.00s (2 ms)  (  0.0%) (residual)\n  Leaf Recursion           0.50s (502 ms)  (  6.5%)\n  Inner Recursion          0.41s (409 ms)  (  5.3%)\n  Compression              0.27s (270 ms)  (  3.5%)\n  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Total                    7.75s (7746 ms)  (100.0%)\n```\n\nWe would expect \"STARK (excl. trace)\" to scale with a combination of cells, bus interaction messages and constraint instances, which are all going down by a factor of >2x when going from 0 to 300 APCs. This is not the case in practice on GPU though.\n\n## Profiling\n\nNVIDIA nsight and nvidia-smi are available. Use them to understand GPU performance characteristics and bottlenecks.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do NOT change the underlying cryptographic protocol.\n- Do NOT change the verifier.\n- Do NOT optimize other proving phases, aside from \"STARK (excl. trace)\"\n\n## Result Files\n\nFor each task, collect:\n- `before_apc{000,100,300}.json` — metrics before the change\n- `after_apc{000,100,300}.json` — metrics after the change\n- `metrics_combined.json` — created using `basic_metrics.py`\n- Relevant profiling files (nsight exports, etc.)\n\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
