tions: Vec<Interaction<usize>> = interactions\n        .iter()\n        .map(|interaction| {\n            let fields: Vec<usize> = interaction\n                .message\n                .iter()\n                .map(|field_expr| builder.add_expr(field_expr))\n                .collect();\n            let count = builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n            Interaction {\n                message: fields,\n                count,\n                bus_index: interaction.bus_index,\n                count_weight: interaction.count_weight,\n            }\n        })\n        .collect();\n    let constraints = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n        nodes: builder.nodes,\n        constraint_idx,\n    };\n    SymbolicConstraintsDag {\n        constraints,\n        interactions,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Builder for constructing a symbolic expression DAG with structural deduplication\n/// and algebraic simplifications.\n///\n/// Two caches are used:\n/// - `expr_to_idx`: Fast path for expressions with the same Arc pointer\n/// - `node_to_idx`: Structural deduplication - catches identical nodes with different Arc pointers\n///\n/// Algebraic simplifications performed:\n/// - Constant folding: `a + b` → `c`, `a - b` → `c`, `a * b` → `c`, `-a` → `c` (for constants a,b)","numLines":60,"startLine":77,"totalLines":741}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GUPFZfnzPg6uMDch8ZXeyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very clear picture. The `SymbolicConstraintsDag` stores interactions as `Vec<Interaction<usize>>` where the `usize` is a node index into the DAG. This is the key insight - the DAG stores interactions with their expression indices already computed.\n\nI can use these pre-existing indices directly from `single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions` (which are `Interaction<usize>`) instead of rebuilding the DAG from scratch. The current code in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` does this:\n\n1. Takes `SymbolicConstraints` (which has `interactions: Vec<SymbolicInteraction<F>>` with full expressions)\n\n\n2. Rebuilds a new DAG by calling `dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count)` and `dag_builder.add_expr(&message)` for each\n3. Creates rules from this DAG\n4. Uses `dag_builder.expr_to_idx` (pointer-keyed) to map back to dag indices for weight computation\n\nBut here's the real problem - the constraints DAG and the interactions DAG are separate, and I need to figure out how to reconcile them when computing weights.\n\nThe solution is to build the interaction-only DAG at keygen time, compile the rules, and precompute the weight map, then store both in the proving key. At proving time, I only need to compute the runtime-dependent weights using that precomputed map. Now let me check how `SymbolicConstraints::from` converts the DAG back to expressions so I understand the full picture.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1458,"cache_read_input_tokens":62225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1458},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dad4735-cfc3-4e7