{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UknUuo1pGabgWMqdFnKzzA","type":"tool_result","content":"# Summary of audit_metrics.py\n\nThis Python script audits OpenVM metrics by recomputing experiment details from JSON files and displaying results for verification against a web UI.\n\n## Key Functions\n\n**Data Loading & Processing:**\n- `load_metrics_dataframes()` - Flattens metric entries and groups them by prefix (app_proof, reth, leaf, internal, compression)\n- `extract_metrics()` - The core computation function that calculates all displayed metrics, mirroring JavaScript logic from index.html\n\n**Metric Calculations:**\n- Sums metrics across AIR instances using `sum_metric()` and `unique_metric()`\n- Classifies AIRs as PowdrAir, normal instructions, or precompiles via `is_normal_instruction_air()`\n- Weights constraints and interactions by segment/row counts\n- Computes proof time breakdowns (execute, STARK, trace, preflight)\n- Calculates cell distribution ratios\n\n**Version Detection:**\nThe script detects OpenVM version (1 or 2) by checking for \"logup_gkr\" metrics, adjusting displayed stats accordingly.\n\n**Display Logic:**\n- V1 includes \"app_proof_cells_used\"; V2 omits it\n- V2 adds detailed STARK sub-components (trace commit, RAP constraints, openings)\n- Proof times shown with indentation hierarchy and residual flagging\n\n**Input Flexibility:**\nAccepts local file paths or HTTP(S) URLs (auto-converting GitHub blob URLs to raw format) and handles both single and combined metrics files."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dad4735-cfc3-4e75-88af-7885288c829c","uuid":"4db02c90-e545-4b18-af59-7789b8c12b80","timestamp":"2026-04-11T08:07:20.120Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":17517,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Summary of audit_metrics.py\n\nThis Python script audits OpenVM metrics by recomputing experiment details from JSON files and displaying results for verification against a web UI.\n\n## Key Functions\n\n**Data Loading & Processing:**\n- `load_metrics_dataframes()` - Flattens metric entries and groups them by prefix (app_proof, reth, leaf, internal, compression)\n- `extract_metrics()` - The core computation function that calculates all displayed metrics, mirroring JavaScript logic from index.html\n\n**Metric Calculations:**\n- Sums metrics across AIR instances using `sum_metric()` and `unique_metric()`\n- Classifies AIRs as PowdrAir, normal instructions, or precompiles via `is_normal_instruction_air()`\n- Weights constraints and interactions by segment/row counts\n- Computes proof time breakdowns (execute, STARK, trace, preflight)\n- Calculates cell distribution ratios\n\n**Version Detection:**\nThe script detects OpenVM version (1 or 2) by checking for \"logup_gkr\" metrics, adjusting displayed stats accordingly.\n\n**Display Logic:**\n- V1 includes \"app_proof_cells_used\"; V2 omits it\n- V2 adds detailed STARK sub-components (trace commit, RAP constraints, openings)\n- Proof times shown with indentation hierarchy and residual flagging\n\n**Input Flexibility:**\nAccepts local file paths or HTTP(S) URLs (auto-converting GitHub blob URLs to raw format) and handles both single and combined metrics files.","durationMs":6281,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/powdr-labs/powdr/refs/heads/main/openvm/metrics-viewer/spec.py"}}
